WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.699
- Welcome back to our
teacher appreciation hour

00:00:02.699 --> 00:00:05.090
and an audience, full of
teachers and students.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.879
We are also with the cast

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:09.162
of Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness.

00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:11.372
Benedict Cumberbatch, Elizabeth Olson,

00:00:11.372 --> 00:00:12.951
Benedict Wong and Xochitl Gomez!

00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:15.489
(audience cheering)

00:00:15.489 --> 00:00:16.342
In the new movie,

00:00:16.342 --> 00:00:19.628
all of these very talented
actors play characters, endowed

00:00:19.628 --> 00:00:21.132
with magical powers.

00:00:21.132 --> 00:00:23.372
I am the only one here without any magic

00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:25.015
and I'm very sad about it.

00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:26.241
I feel like I have magic deep inside.

00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:27.712
- You're a kick-ass musician
of the highest order.

00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:28.545
- See, thank you!

00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:29.631
- That is a magic power.

00:00:29.631 --> 00:00:30.720
(everyone applauding)

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.693
- Thank you, a super power.

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:34.409
Anyway, to celebrate Doctor Strange

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:35.947
and all things magical, it is time

00:00:35.947 --> 00:00:38.005
for a game called, That'll Do The Trick.

00:00:38.005 --> 00:00:39.605
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.855
♪ That'll do the trick ♪

00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:47.721
So, teams are The Benedicts
versus The Winners.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.015
- [Benedict] Oh, it's like that?

00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:50.848
- Yeah, it's on, oh yeah, it's on.

00:00:50.848 --> 00:00:51.681
- Oh, oh, oh, okay.

00:00:51.681 --> 00:00:52.710
- [Kelly] I'm very competitive.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.662
- Glad my sleeves are already
rolled up, yeah, all right.

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:56.403
- C and W better be ready.

00:00:56.403 --> 00:00:58.342
And to host, let's call upon the man

00:00:58.342 --> 00:01:00.711
with the magical voice,
Lord are you there?

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:02.235
- [Host] I am here, how you doing Kelly?

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:03.208
- I'm so good.

00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:05.128
- [Host] Hey Elizabeth, hey Benedict W,

00:01:05.128 --> 00:01:07.781
hey Xochitl, hey Briar
Patch, how you all doing?

00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:09.160
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.703
- Good thanks, God.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.536
- [Host] Very good to see you.

00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:14.604
Here we go Briar Patch, here's
how today's game works, okay?

00:01:14.604 --> 00:01:18.073
I'm gonna ask a question
that has to do with magic.

00:01:18.073 --> 00:01:19.235
Now, it might be from a story,

00:01:19.235 --> 00:01:22.797
might be a real life magician,
it might be a magic trick.

00:01:22.797 --> 00:01:24.971
Now, if you know the answer, buzz in.

00:01:24.971 --> 00:01:27.404
Now, you may buzz in before
I finish the question

00:01:27.404 --> 00:01:31.084
but then, you will not hear
the rest of the question.

00:01:31.084 --> 00:01:31.917
- Fine.

00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:35.446
- [Host] And, if you are
wrong, steals are allowed.

00:01:35.446 --> 00:01:36.279
- Ooh.

00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:37.112
- Steals.

00:01:37.112 --> 00:01:37.945
- [Host] That's right.

00:01:37.945 --> 00:01:40.225
Now, if The Benedicts win,
their photo will go up

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:41.685
on the not so magical,

00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:45.354
Blake Shelton Wall of Champions
who beat Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:45.354 --> 00:01:46.187
- [Kelly] Stupid wall.

00:01:46.187 --> 00:01:47.818
- [Host] That's my
favorite wall in the world.

00:01:47.818 --> 00:01:48.765
- Stupid wall!

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:49.919
Stupid wall!

00:01:49.919 --> 00:01:51.125
(contestants laughing)

00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:52.586
- [Host] Here we go.

00:01:52.586 --> 00:01:55.733
The first question is, who was the name

00:01:55.733 --> 00:01:57.375
of the magician who served

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:59.614
in King Arthur's?
(buzzer ringing)

00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:00.998
- Merlin.

00:02:00.998 --> 00:02:02.526
- [Host] It was Merlin.

00:02:02.526 --> 00:02:04.062
- How did you know it already?

00:02:04.062 --> 00:02:04.895
- [Host] That's right.

00:02:04.895 --> 00:02:05.728
(audience applauding)

00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:08.497
- The full question, wasn't even there!

00:02:08.497 --> 00:02:10.021
- It's slightly terrifying, really.

00:02:10.021 --> 00:02:10.854
- [Xochitl] This is so sad.

00:02:10.854 --> 00:02:11.687
- You know you hit the buzzer you're like-

00:02:11.687 --> 00:02:12.550
- I knew that was gonna be Merlin

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:15.132
but he didn't even to
the full, whatever Wong.

00:02:15.132 --> 00:02:16.303
- I pressed the buzzer

00:02:16.303 --> 00:02:19.910
and then I made him say
it, isn't that amazing?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.743
That'll do the trick.

00:02:20.743 --> 00:02:21.576
- That's how we do it.

00:02:21.576 --> 00:02:22.694
- That'll do the trick.

00:02:22.694 --> 00:02:25.510
- WC, no, no, CW, WC sounds wrong.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:26.818
- [Kelly] We are not doing well!

00:02:26.818 --> 00:02:27.751
- [Host] That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:27.751 --> 00:02:28.769
- I'm not good at trivia,
y'all, I'm so sorry.

00:02:28.769 --> 00:02:30.752
- [Host] All right, CW,
come on now, ladies.

00:02:30.752 --> 00:02:32.300
Here we go, let's get it together.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.070
Here's your next question.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.109
Next question is, in what animated movie

00:02:37.109 --> 00:02:40.532
was the magical antagonist named Jafar?

00:02:40.532 --> 00:02:41.823
- Oh, Aladdin!

00:02:41.823 --> 00:02:42.656
(buzzer dinging)

00:02:42.656 --> 00:02:43.489
- [Host] It was Aladdin!

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:45.665
(everyone applauding)

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.748
There you go.

00:02:48.712 --> 00:02:50.988
- You go ahead with that
Disney stuff, I got that.

00:02:50.988 --> 00:02:52.978
- [Host] Uh-huh, well, that's
the last one we gonna do then.

00:02:52.978 --> 00:02:55.175
Okay, here you go.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.330
Here's the next question,
get ready for it.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.298
This is goin' be a tough one.

00:02:58.298 --> 00:02:59.293
- Okay.

00:02:59.293 --> 00:03:01.661
- In the Marvel cinematic universe,

00:03:01.661 --> 00:03:04.455
what mischievous character shares a name

00:03:04.455 --> 00:03:07.421
with a magical shapeshifting...

00:03:07.421 --> 00:03:08.327
- [Duo] Loki.

00:03:08.327 --> 00:03:09.160
- [Host] It is Loki!
(bell dinging)

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.640
- [Kelly] I love it when we're right!

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.557
(audience cheering)

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:12.795
- [Host] Okay, here's the next one, okay?

00:03:12.795 --> 00:03:16.688
Now, in what Shakespeare
play, do the Weird Sisters

00:03:16.688 --> 00:03:17.687
also known...
(buzzer ringing)

00:03:17.687 --> 00:03:18.520
- Macbeth.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.353
- The Scottish Play.

00:03:19.353 --> 00:03:20.186
- [Host] It is,
(bell dinging)

00:03:20.186 --> 00:03:21.248
(audience cheering)

00:03:21.248 --> 00:03:22.762
the Scottish Play, thank you for saying-

00:03:22.762 --> 00:03:25.139
- [Kelly] Of course,
he's English, we're good.

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:26.309
- [Elizabeth] Whatever.

00:03:26.309 --> 00:03:27.142
- Whatever.

00:03:27.142 --> 00:03:27.975
- Whatever I don't care.

00:03:27.975 --> 00:03:28.808
- Bitter.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.391
(horn blaring)

00:03:32.282 --> 00:03:33.135
- Is this a double?

00:03:33.135 --> 00:03:34.042
- This is br-br-br.

00:03:34.042 --> 00:03:35.331
- [Host] This is, for double the points,

00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:36.600
it is our final question.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.433
- Never played this before,

00:03:37.433 --> 00:03:38.786
but I knew it was a double.

00:03:38.786 --> 00:03:39.619
- [Host] Now, this is your big chance.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.960
This is your big chance,
Benedicts, so get ready.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.893
- Come one Shakespeare.

00:03:43.893 --> 00:03:44.747
(Elizabeth chuckling)

00:03:44.747 --> 00:03:46.142
- [Host] And, I appreciate
you saying The Scottish Play

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.469
by the way, otherwise it
would've cursed all of our asses.

00:03:48.469 --> 00:03:49.302
Okay, here we go now.

00:03:49.302 --> 00:03:50.135
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:50.135 --> 00:03:51.999
Next question, the final question.

00:03:51.999 --> 00:03:56.125
What is the name of the
cape worn by Doctor Strange?

00:03:56.125 --> 00:03:56.958
(buzzer dinging)

00:03:56.958 --> 00:03:57.791
- Oh!

00:03:58.663 --> 00:03:59.496
- Name of the cape.

00:03:59.496 --> 00:04:00.329
- Oh dang it!

00:04:00.329 --> 00:04:01.162
- I know this!

00:04:01.162 --> 00:04:01.995
- Dang it!

00:04:01.995 --> 00:04:02.828
- It's a cloak.

00:04:02.828 --> 00:04:03.728
- It's a cloak.

00:04:03.728 --> 00:04:04.644
- No, it's a cloak but it's-

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:05.612
- It's okay, Cloak of Levitation.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.722
- Oh!

00:04:06.722 --> 00:04:07.563
- Cloak of Levitation!

00:04:07.563 --> 00:04:08.396
(buzzer dinging)

00:04:08.396 --> 00:04:09.229
- Yes!

00:04:09.229 --> 00:04:10.062
- What just happened?

00:04:10.062 --> 00:04:10.940
We gotta do another round.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.946
(everyone laughing)

00:04:12.946 --> 00:04:14.055
(buzzer dinging)

00:04:14.055 --> 00:04:16.924
- [Host] It is the Cloak of Levitation.

00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:18.924
God says that's correct.

00:04:19.783 --> 00:04:20.616
(audience cheering)
(horn blaring)

00:04:20.616 --> 00:04:22.778
- Oh, that's gotta
hurt, that's gotta hurt.

00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:25.778
(audience cheering)

00:04:26.645 --> 00:04:29.775
- Oh my gosh, this was actually
my favorite part of this,

00:04:29.775 --> 00:04:31.418
"What happened, well, we've
gotta do another round."

00:04:31.418 --> 00:04:32.909
(everyone laughing)

00:04:32.909 --> 00:04:34.575
She sensed our loss.

00:04:34.575 --> 00:04:35.408
- I know.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.241
- No, no!

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:37.455
- Okay, whatever.

00:04:37.455 --> 00:04:39.140
How did I get that wrong?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:40.130
- I don't know if I've ever-

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.090
- I've never heard that
name before in my life.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.194
- I don't know if I've
ever really paid attention

00:04:43.194 --> 00:04:44.898
to the, I'm very mad at myself right now.

00:04:44.898 --> 00:04:46.317
- [Benedict] He's your favorite character.

00:04:46.317 --> 00:04:48.410
- I know, my mom is
gonna, you have no idea,

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.676
she's gonna be like,
"You're a disappointment."

00:04:52.676 --> 00:04:53.764
- Do they really call it that?

00:04:53.764 --> 00:04:54.906
- When do you call it that?

00:04:54.906 --> 00:04:55.852
- The Cloak of Levitation.

00:04:55.852 --> 00:04:58.273
- When it gets, on my back.

00:04:58.273 --> 00:04:59.106
- [Kelly] No!

00:04:59.106 --> 00:05:00.500
- Yeah.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.849
It's called Cloak, as well
as Cloak of Levitation.

00:05:02.849 --> 00:05:03.682
- I said Cloak!

00:05:03.682 --> 00:05:04.515
- But, it's a cloak,

00:05:04.515 --> 00:05:05.348
but I didn't know it was like, whatever!

00:05:05.348 --> 00:05:06.181
- Not a cloak, it's the cloak.

00:05:06.181 --> 00:05:07.425
- [Xochitl] I could've
gotten a half a point.

00:05:07.425 --> 00:05:08.523
- You know what, you know what?

00:05:08.523 --> 00:05:09.356
- [Benedict] Yeah.

00:05:09.356 --> 00:05:11.008
- Since Team Benedict won,

00:05:11.008 --> 00:05:12.011
their picture will be placed

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.152
on this dumb wall called,

00:05:13.152 --> 00:05:15.765
The Blake Shelton Wall of
Champions who beat Kelly Clarkson.

00:05:15.765 --> 00:05:17.119
(audience cheering)

00:05:17.119 --> 00:05:19.648
I wish I could use magic
to make it disappear.

00:05:19.648 --> 00:05:20.481
- [Benedict] Feels good, it feels good.

00:05:20.481 --> 00:05:21.348
(audience applauding)

